    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I wanted to reproduce the example here: <a href=\"https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/devel/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/advanceTreeAnnotation.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/devel/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/advanceTreeAnnotation.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482883171000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1adBtDG5x34dCAZxep9E3_\">https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/devel/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/advanceTreeAnnotation.html</a> under &quot;Plot Tree with associated data&quot;. However, I could not find the facet_plot function and it doesn&#39;t seem to be included in ggplot2/ gtree anymore.<div><br></div><div>So I tried this:<br><div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><div>library(ggtree)</div><div><br></div><div>tr &lt;- rtree(30)</div><div><br></div><div>p1 &lt;- ggtree(tr)</div><div>d1 &lt;- data.frame(id=tr$tip.label, val=rnorm(30, sd=3))</div><div>p2 &lt;- ggplot(d1, aes(x=id, y=val)) + geom_point() + coord_flip()</div><div>multiplot(p1 + geom_tiplab(), p2, ncol =2 )</div></font></div></code></div><br>How do I align the tip labels of the tree and the labels of the scatterplot/ or can I somehow adjust the plot size? In the example under the link, it seemed to adjust the height of the plots. Also, is it possible to sort the scatterplot according to the tip.label?</div></div></div><div><br></div><div> Is there maybe a ggtree internal function for this?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance!e</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div></font></span></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
